    mission: { situation: 'You are Haru. Your tutor is Aiko. Listen to her new message after the discussion. Confirm which questions you should ask before choosing a management arrangement.', task: 'Explain the possible division, name two factors to check, and distinguish discussion from commitment.', roles: ['Aiko', 'Haru'], title: 'Questions before choosing a role', text: 'Haru, before you decide, ask which daily tasks you could coordinate and who might teach the specialist skills. Check how that would affect your other projects and the workshop’s running costs. No one has agreed to a teaching role yet. The point is to explore a practical division, rather than assume that one person must manage, teach and fund everything. Keep the alternatives open until those questions are clearer.', lines: ['Haru, which responsibilities might be separated?', 'Who could you ask about specialist teaching?', 'What should you check about your own projects?', 'Why do running costs belong in the decision?', 'Has anyone committed to a teaching role yet?', 'What needs to become clearer before you choose?'], evidence: 'Fresh message supplies the next questions and confirms no teaching commitments at this stage. Closure is an eventual alternative, not a decided action. Do not invent salaries, paid roles, a signed agreement or a full-time management appointment. A clear comparison and questions about feasibility satisfy the task.', useful: ['One option is ...', 'We should take ... into account.', 'We could divide ...', 'Before I decide, I need to ...', 'Nothing has been agreed yet.'] },
