    mission: { situation: 'You are Haru. Your tutor is Aiko. Read the new caption-planning note. Decide what the exhibition can accurately say about the photograph and the workshop’s history.', task: 'Correct the age, attribute the recollections, and explain the community connection.', roles: ['Aiko', 'Haru'], title: 'Caption planning note', text: '<p><strong>Caption planning: apprentice photograph</strong></p><p>Use nineteen as Mrs. Takeda’s age. “About twenty” was Daniel’s guess before she corrected it. The interview does not supply a calendar year for the photograph.</p><p>Present the difficult periods as her recollections: slow business, artisans leaving and difficulty finding apprentices. Do not describe her career as effortless.</p><p>Her key point is that the workshop belongs within a wider community of makers and learners. The display should help visitors understand those connections.</p><p>Daniel has permission to photograph the historical materials. That is not an agreement from every person for every future use of a photograph. Check any further proposed use separately.</p>', lines: ['Haru, what age belongs in the caption?', 'Can we add a calendar year from the information given?', 'Which difficulties did your grandmother recall?', 'How should we make clear whose memories these are?', 'What would a one-person success story leave out?', 'Does this permission cover every possible future use?'], evidence: 'Fresh note makes the age correction and missing year explicit. Personal testimony is attributed. Keep permission specific to photographing these materials; do not invent a public archive licence or consent from all people pictured. Do not assume Haru has taken over yet or that the exhibition already includes every colleague’s story.', useful: ['She said she was ...', 'The photograph does not tell us ...', 'She recalled ...', 'This puts ... in context.', 'The workshop is part of ...'] },
    topics: [['PERSONAL HISTORIES', ['What can a photograph show and leave unexplained?', 'Why attribute a memory to its speaker?', 'How can you correct a detail respectfully?']], ['SHARED LEGACIES', ['Who can be overlooked in a success story?', 'Why does a craft need a community?', 'Can a new generation contribute without copying every detail?']], ['HISTORICAL DISPLAYS', ['What makes a caption useful?', 'What should you do when a date is unknown?', 'Why check permission for a new use?']]],
